{
  "_what": "The cabin behind the door marked E: its two pages and the rack beside its record player. Read by tools/make-secret-cabin.py, which draws the door, the lights and the turntable, writes the rack and the door's word, and refuses what this room refuses. Both pages are unlisted (tools/unlisted.py): nothing on the street links to them and no list names them.",
  "_source": "Ryan's brief, 2026-10-07, and his addition the same day. Every album was read that day off its artist's own YouTube channel, whose Releases tab lists it as a playlist; every song was opened on its own watch page and answered playabilityStatus OK and playableInEmbed true, on one of that artist's channels (its own, its Topic channel or its VEVO channel). `seconds` is what plays, read off the playlist; `record` is the same song's length on the record, read off a MusicBrainz release of that album the same day; and where the two differ by more than a few seconds, or what plays is a film or another version, `plays` says so on the back of the sleeve. The years and labels are MusicBrainz's. Titles are the record's, as MusicBrainz lists them. The rack is in the order Ryan named them.",
  "door": "the-secret-cabin.html",
  "inside": "lydtyss.html",
  "words_by": "anonymous",
  "_words_by": "Ryan's call, 2026-10-07: the words are printed as they were given, and the cabin names nobody as their author. Whose hand wrote them is not said anywhere in the room, on purpose, and neither is whose brief it was.",
